## 📚 Key Concepts

| Concept | Description |
|---|---|
| **Network Policy** | A Kubernetes resource that controls allowed traffic flows between pods |
| **Ingress Policy** | Rules governing which sources are allowed to send traffic into a pod |
| **Egress Policy** | Rules governing which destinations a pod is allowed to send traffic to |
| **Layered (Tiered) Security** | Restricting traffic by application tier — e.g., frontend → backend → database only |
| **Microsegmentation** | Isolating individual workloads to limit the impact of a compromised pod |
| **Zero Trust Networking** | A security model where no traffic is trusted by default, and access must be explicitly allowed |
| **Namespace-Based Policy** | A Network Policy scoped to control traffic across or within specific namespaces |

